 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? That' a common mistake. People often start with the eyeball too high up on the face. About halfway is a good rule of thumb. Start with the line from the nose to the bottom lip on the side of the face, and draw an eyeball about halfway up that line. The nose should point slightly towards the person's cheek. If you draw the line from the nose to the lip, the nose should be bit turned to the side. Have fun with it. Rough drawings with people you like are great way to get used to the basics.",
